Z||000001||qwikgta||08-12-2001||06:15 PM||||Check with the sport compact car crowd, they are in to this.  Some work has been done in the Sunfire/Cavelier crowd, they too like to get low.  They may have a way to do the struts in the back.  <P>AS for the front, 84-87 models have the offset shock/spring combo that most kits use.  If you replece the front spring with a bag you just have to figure out the strut in the back.  Good luck<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
