Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-12-2001||08:20 PM||||I know the principles behind air bags, but wouldn't it be logical to think that if you lowered the car with bags, you would ride more like a Cadillac than a Porsche?  No (or very little) air would make for a soft ride, right?  Where's the performance gain?  Or would this be for looks only?<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000004||baggedlowrider||08-14-2001||05:01 PM||||the bags are just for looks i want to be able to drop it at lights and mess around i dont care about the ride if anything it will make the ride stiffer!!!!! but do you know where i can  get a kit for the rear?||||reg||5
Z||000005||qwikgta||08-14-2001||10:30 PM||||Where I was going with my thread is that I have seen pics in the mags of bag installs.  The idea seems to be to replace the spring with a bag setup, now some suspentions do not have the spring/shock setup as a combo.  The 84-87 front end is an example.  The spring is in one place the shock next to it.  So if you remove the spring and insert a bag then put back on the shock you are good to go.  <P>In the rear (of all fieros 84-88) they have Mcpherson struts.  I think "they" have a bag system for the struts, don't quote me on that, that is what you will have to look up in the Sport Compact Car mags.  As I understand the "*****" crowd uses struts, so if they have a bag system on their ride they have figured it out.  <P>Good luck<P>Rob<P>||||reg||1
